having seen the 1993 Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
having seen Kret dated November 1, 1993 on the appointment of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
upon the proposal of the two Prime Ministers and the Ministers of Health.
Promulgate.
General Provision
This Kram has an objective to determine procedures and conditions for abortion.
"Abortion", means a termination of a fetus by medicinal or any other method.
Only medical doctors, medium medical practitioners or midwives who received authorization from the Ministry of Public Health may perform the abortion.
Procedures and Conditions for Abortion
Abortion may be carried out only inside a hospital, health center, public or private clinic or maternity which is authorized by Ministry of Public Health.
a technical capability in providing emergency medical treatment for any consequence which may result from abortion.
Means of transportation to a hospital, if necessary.
there is a probable cause that such fetus does not develop itself as usual or which may cause danger to the mother's life.
Technical conditions for application of this article shall be determined by a Proclamation (Prakas) of the Ministry of Health.
Controlling / Inspecting Competence
The control / inspection of abortion shall be the competence of the Ministry of Public Health.
shall be subject to a reprimand if such person is a medical doctor, medium medical practitioner or midwife.
Except only in serious cases, where the pregnant woman needs to have an emergency operation, the medicinal method shall be applied and be responsible before the law.
If he / she is a government servant, shall receive punishment pursuant to the articles 40 and 41 of the Kram on Common Statutes of the Civil Servants.
Final Provision
Those provisions which are contrary to this Kram shall be hereby abrogated.
This Kram is passed by the National Assembly of the Kingdom of Cambodia, on October 6, 1997, during its 8th Ordinary Session of the 1st Legislature.
